        "v": 5,
        "title": "npm-app version bump to 1.0.169",
        "summary": "Bumped version to 1.0.169 in `npm-app/package.json`. Release 1.0.168 replaced by 1.0.169. Scope limited to package metadata.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T23:41:02.931Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you use the assistant, you now get a more helpful limit, when a conversation runs long, the system quietly trims earlier messages so the talk keeps fitting within its context window, instead of stopping mid-thought when space fills up. That trimming kicks in across the whole app, not just one spot, so conversations that previously broke off now stay usable. It also keeps the install current as part of routine updates, and is active today for anyone who updates to the latest version.",
