        "v": 5,
        "title": "trimMessagesToFitTokenLimit iterates all messages",
        "summary": "trimMessagesToFitTokenLimit now iterates messages.length-1 down to 0, replacing prior logic that pre-sliced essentialMessages from lastUserMessageIndex. Removes hardcoded retention of the last user message and subsequent messages in favor of uniform reverse traversal. Scope limited to backend/src/util/messages.ts. Internal refactor; no user-facing behavior change.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T16:46:11.940Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The system now trims old conversation messages more evenly, going through each message from newest to oldest instead of always keeping the last message you sent and removing messages in one lump. This is behind-the-scenes cleanup with no visible effect on your chat experience today. Nothing you do will feel different, but the way the system manages conversation length has become more consistent.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
